# Keep the Docker build context small. All three images build from the repo root:
#   Dockerfile                  → the landing (apps/site/)
#   Dockerfile.plans-explorer   → the explorer (apps/data/projects/ + apps/plans-explorer/)
#   Dockerfile.submission-api   → the write path (apps/submission-api/ + the schema)
#
# Nothing here is required by either build. Excluding node_modules matters most:
# the image runs `npm ci` itself, and shipping a host-built tree into the context
# is both slow and wrong (native modules built for the wrong platform).

.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Generated by the indexer inside the image; a host copy would mask a broken build.
apps/plans-explorer/app/dist
apps/plans-explorer/app/public/data
apps/plans-explorer/app/public/projects
apps/plans-explorer/app/.cache

# Scraper state and its cache — the build is offline, enriched plans own their prose.
apps/data/tools/problemhunt-scraper/node_modules
apps/data/tools/problemhunt-scraper/state.json*
apps/data/tools/problemhunt-scraper/last-run.log

# Local environment and secrets. Never in an image layer.
dev-env/env-config/.env
dev-env/env-config.zip
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Repo-side material neither image serves.
archive
outputs
specs
vendor
memory
docs
prompts
setup
skills
ai-config
context
rules
verifiers
workflows
apps/plans-explorer/app/node_modules

# Product material that is not an image input. A bare `outputs` above matches only the
# root-level one, so the plans product's own outputs dir needs naming explicitly — it is
# 3.7 MB of generated run artifacts that would otherwise ride along in every build context.
apps/data/outputs
apps/data/progress
apps/data/skills
apps/create-ai-os

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
*.log
.claude
